{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>It shall be broken.</b> Because the blialah that is absorbed in it becomes notar — and the same law applies to all consecrated offerings." "<b>And scoured.</b> A term of women's cosmetics (Esther 2); אשקור\"מנט בְּלַעַז." "<b>And scoured and rinsed.</b> To release its blialah — but an earthenware vessel the verse teaches you here that it never leaves the domain of its dafyon (Avodah Zarah 34)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French escurumant, 'scouring/cleaning agent'", 2 "blialah refers to the absorbed sacrificial matter; dafyon is Rashi's term for the vessel's absorbed flavor, here rendered by transliteration since no single English word captures it precisely"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:16.405822644Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}